  "text": "In March 2022, most of us turned to one occasion. Fifty-three of us said \"state of the union\"; fifty of us said \"state of the union address.\" We were speaking around one night, and the record shows how we kept to it.\n\nThen we dispersed into the year's bills. Twenty-eight of us said \"community project funding.\" Twenty-five of us said \"the honoring our pact act,\" and twenty of us said \"exposed to toxic.\" Twenty-four of us said \"the affordable insulin now act\"; twenty-three of us said \"35 per month.\"\n\nTwenty-three of us also said \"1 000 000,\" though the record here does not say of what.\n\nThis was our convergence: one night, then bills, each carried by dozens of us at once.",
